    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n2736" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">antĕ-ambŭlo</span></b>  (in poetry four
		syll.), ōnis, m.
		ambulo, āre, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a forerunner</i>, <i>a servant
				that went before distinguished personages to clear the way</i>,
			etc.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">anteambulo regis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mart.
					2, 18, 5</span></i>
			; so <i><span class="en">id. 10, 74, 3</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Suet.
				Vesp. 2</span></i>.</div>
